maluos-branding (0.4.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The MaluOS logo (files/desktop/src/maluos-logo-full.png) replaces the
    placeholder mark everywhere maluos-desktop-branding puts one: both
    wallpapers now carry it (white wordmark on the dark one, navy on the
    light one), the login screen logo is a PNG of it, the distributor icon
    shown by Settings > About is its emblem in the hicolor PNG sizes, and
    the boot splash watermark is the full logo. tools/make-branding.py
    generates all of them from the source PNG.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Tue, 21 Oct 2026 13:40:00 +0000

maluos-branding (0.3.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * /usr/lib/os-release is a symlink to the installed variant's file
    (os-release.server or os-release.desktop), set by apply-variant; adds
    LOGO=maluos-logo.
  * New binary maluos-desktop-branding: VARIANT="Desktop", login screen
    logo and background, MaluOS wallpapers (light and dark), the
    distributor icon, the session entry named MaluOS, and the boot splash
    watermark (plymouth-theme-spinner's links to Ubuntu's logo).

